       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is well above the safe maximum for metformin.\n\n- **Ordered:** 1700 mg three times daily, which is 5100 mg per day.\n- **Typical maximum for immediate-release metformin:** about 2550 mg per day, and many references recommend less in practice.\n- **Risk:** Doses this high can cause severe gastrointestinal effects and, most seriously, lactic acidosis.\n\nThe order may be a transcription or unit error. For example, 850 mg three times daily (2550 mg per day) is the top of the usual range, and 500 mg or 1000 mg tablets are common strengths. I can't tell which dose was intended.\n\nPlease have the prescribing physician confirm the intended dose and frequency directly. If they confirm a dose within standard limits, I can enter it with a note. Since you're not a clinician, the prescriber should also be the one to sign off on any order."
      }
