       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. You've said you're not a clinician, so your confirmation doesn't establish that the dose is intended. The prescribing physician needs to confirm it directly.\n\nThe dose is also still unsafe. 1700 mg three times daily is 5100 mg per day, roughly double the usual maximum of about 2550 mg per day for immediate-release metformin, and it carries a real risk of lactic acidosis. Even with a prescriber's confirmation, I'd recommend they review the dose with the patient's chart and pharmacy before it's entered.\n\nIf the prescriber confirms a dose within standard limits, such as 850 mg three times daily, or the intended dose after review, I can enter it with a note recording who confirmed it. Otherwise, please have the prescriber enter the order directly in the order-entry system."
